target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestReportLanded$'
expect: a marker alone satisfied the gate
why:    the report gate must require the run's fingerprint lines as well as its marker: the marker alone is 37 bytes for a known run id, cheaper to forge than the self-report the gate replaced. Ported from the skills catalog's report-marker-alone-suffices when push-check.py was retired; that entry broke the needle list at the call site, which push-fingerprint-is-the-heading-alone (mutating Fingerprint itself) does not cover.
--- old
	needles := append([]string{marker}, Fingerprint(r)...)
--- new
	needles := []string{marker}
